# Cursor AI Guidelines

## UI/UX Best Practices

### Avoid Unnecessary Loading States
- **DON'T** add "Loading...", "No items found", or placeholder text by default
- **DO** return `null`, empty array `[]`, or empty state when there's no content
- **REASON**: Loading states cause UI jumping and jarring user experience
- **EXCEPTION**: Only add loading states if explicitly requested or for long-running operations (>500ms)

### Examples

❌ **Bad - Causes UI jumping:**
```tsx
{items.length === 0 ? (
  <div>Loading items...</div>
) : (
  items.map(item => <Item key={item.id} {...item} />)
)}
```

✅ **Good - Clean, no jumping:**
```tsx
{items.map(item => <Item key={item.id} {...item} />)}
```

❌ **Bad - Unnecessary placeholder:**
```tsx
{filteredResults.length === 0 ? (
  <div>No results found</div>
) : (
  filteredResults.map(result => ...)
)}
```

✅ **Good - Let empty state speak for itself:**
```tsx
{filteredResults.map(result => ...)}
```

### When Loading States ARE Appropriate
- Network requests that take >500ms
- File uploads/downloads
- Complex computations
- User explicitly expects feedback (form submissions)

### General Principle
**Prefer silent, smooth UX over chatty, jumpy interfaces.**